# 13. SYSTEM TESTING AND LIVE DEMONSTRATION

This module is CRITICAL.

Create a complete interactive system testing page based on the eight test cases in page 12 of the reference PDF.

Provide the following test scenarios:

TEST 1: NORMAL WI-FI COMMUNICATION
- Node 1 Wi-Fi ON.
- Node 1 LoRa READY.
- Node 2 → Node 3 Wi-Fi ON.
- Packet transmitted to Node 2.
- Gateway stores packet.
- Node 1 receives matching ACK.
- Node 2 forwards encrypted packet.
- Node 3 authenticates and decrypts.
- Node 3 sends ACK.
- Final result: DELIVERED.

TEST 2: WI-FI FAILURE WITH LORA FALLBACK
- Node 1 Wi-Fi OFF.
- Node 1 LoRa ON.
- Node 2 → Node 3 Wi-Fi ON.
- Packet transmitted over LoRa.
- Gateway stores packet.
- Gateway sends LoRa ACK.
- Node 2 forwards to Node 3.
- Final result: DELIVERED.

TEST 3: BOTH NODE 1 LINKS UNAVAILABLE
- Node 1 Wi-Fi OFF.
- Node 1 LoRa OFF.
- Node 1 stores packet in LittleFS.
- Sensor sampling continues.
- Restore communication.
- Pending packet is transmitted.
- Matching ACK is received.
- Final result: DELIVERED AFTER RECOVERY.

TEST 4: NODE 3 UNAVAILABLE
- Node 1 → Node 2 link ON.
- Node 2 → Node 3 link OFF.
- Node 2 stores packet on microSD.
- Node 1 receives storage ACK.
- Node 3 pending queue increases.
- Restore Node 3 connectivity.
- Packet is forwarded.
- Node 3 sends ACK.
- Final result: DELIVERED AFTER RECOVERY.

TEST 5: ALL COMMUNICATION LINKS UNAVAILABLE
- Node 1 → Node 2 Wi-Fi OFF.
- Node 1 → Node 2 LoRa OFF.
- Node 2 → Node 3 Wi-Fi OFF.
- Node 1 retains packets in LittleFS.
- Node 2 retains previously received packets in microSD.
- No packet is falsely marked delivered.
- Final result: PENDING / STORED SAFELY.

TEST 6: ACK LOSS AND DUPLICATE DETECTION
- Send a packet.
- Simulate lost ACK.
- Retransmit the same packet ID and ciphertext.
- Node 2 detects duplicate.
- Node 2 does not store/process a second copy.
- Node 2 resends the matching ACK.
- Final result: DUPLICATE SUPPRESSED.

TEST 7: AES-GCM TAMPERING
- Send encrypted packet.
- Modify ciphertext or authentication tag.
- Node 3 verifies the authentication tag.
- Authentication fails.
- Packet is rejected.
- No valid plaintext is displayed.
- No successful destination ACK is sent.
- Final result: SECURITY REJECTION.

TEST 8: NODE RESTART WITH PENDING PACKETS
- Generate pending packets.
- Simulate node restart.
- Recover persistent queues.
- Restore packet IDs and delivery state.
- Resume transmission.
- Final result: PENDING PACKETS RECOVERED.

